cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this addon, cite the entities-godot-cineform tree it is built from and the CineForm SDK it encodes with.
title: godot-cineform, the CineForm exporter for Godot's Movie Maker (vendored binary)
abstract: >-
  V-Sekai-fire/entities-godot-cineform at bf4cf04a02924495d1c6168dd3ab52c72ad02532
  (2026-09-22): a GDExtension MovieWriter that claims the .cfhd output extension
  and writes CineForm (CFHD) frames, 12-bit RGB 4:4:4 at quality 0..5, plus the
  48 kHz stereo PCM track, into a RIFF/AVI container, encoded with the org fork
  of the CineForm SDK (V-Sekai-fire/cineform-sdk at 9c2973f, the LLVM-fixed
  build). Vendored here as three libraries: the Windows x86_64 release DLL
  (bin/libgodot_cineform.windows.template_release.x86_64.dll, 3,484,160 bytes,
  built with clang 23) and the Linux x86_64 template_debug and template_release
  shared objects (bin/libgodot_cineform.linux.template_{debug,release}.x86_64.so,
  6,884,008 and 4,649,000 bytes; sha256 563d4675...93b7 and bd203eda...dcbc),
  built 2026-09-25 on Ubuntu 24.04 with clang 18.1.3 via
  `cmake -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug|Release -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5`
  with godot-cpp at 4bc6e67 and cineform-sdk at 9c2973f under thirdparty/, then
  `strip --strip-debug`. So the loop can be recorded with
  `godot --write-movie <file>.cfhd --fixed-fps 30` (gates/8-loop, the
  dress-on-fit recording of 2026-09-23: 1276 frames, 1152x648, 199 MB).
  Local adaptations: cineform.gdextension maps the windows.debug and
  windows.editor entries to the same release DLL, because the editor binary
  (godot.console.exe) loads the debug/editor entry and no Windows debug build is
  shipped. The Linux build patches one line of the tree's CMakeLists.txt:
  `target_link_options(... -static)` cannot link a shared object against a
  static glibc, so on Linux it links only libstdc++ and libgcc statically and
  links libuuid (the SDK's encoder calls uuid_generate; Debian's libuuid.a is not
  PIC) and pthread dynamically. The .so files need glibc 2.38 or newer
  (Ubuntu 24.04+) and libuuid.so.1. Checked with Godot 4.7.2 on Linux:
  MovieWriterCineForm registers and a 30-frame --write-movie run writes a
  RIFF/AVI .cfhd. The macOS entries name libraries that are not vendored.
  Encoded recordings are transcoded to AV1 in Matroska by tools/av1mkv
  (branch tool-av1mkv), never by FFmpeg.
authors:
  - name: K. S. Ernest (iFire) Lee
  - name: V-Sekai
repository-code: https://github.com/V-Sekai-fire/entities-godot-cineform
